{
  "id": "Compound::DB00253 - Gene::2908",
  "verbalization": "Medrysone, a corticosteroid, is implicated in the interaction with Nr3c1 through multiple pathways that converge on the corticosteroid hormone receptor family. The evidence suggests that Medrysone binds to Serpina6 or Halobetasol Propionate, which in turn binds to Nr3c1, establishing a direct interaction pathway. This is further supported by the inclusion of Medrysone in the category of corticosteroid hormone receptor agonists, which includes Desonide, another corticosteroid that directly binds to Nr3c1. The shared lowest common ancestors—Medrysone and the corticosteroid hormones—highlight the role of corticosteroids in modulating Nr3c1 activity. The integration of these pathways underscores a mechanism by which Medrysone, through its interaction with corticosteroid hormones, may influence Nr3c1, potentially affecting gene expression or cellular signaling. The consistent presence of corticosteroid hormones in the pathway suggests a broader role in the regulation of Nr3c1, aligning with the known function of Nr3c1 as a receptor for corticosteroids.",
